(177, 1, '2026-02-04 13:43:59', '2026-02-04 13:43:59', '<img width=\"1024\" height=\"615\" src=\"http://localhost/zeliigcaretheme/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/anxiety_003-1024x615.jpg\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"http://localhost/zeliigcaretheme/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/anxiety_003-1024x615.jpg 1024w, http://localhost/zeliigcaretheme/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/anxiety_003-300x180.jpg 300w, http://localhost/zeliigcaretheme/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/anxiety_003-768x462.jpg 768w, http://localhost/zeliigcaretheme/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/anxiety_003-1536x923.jpg 1536w, http://localhost/zeliigcaretheme/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/anxiety_003-2048x1231.jpg 2048w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\" />																<h3>Understanding Anxiety</h3>		<p>Anxiety is more than occasional worry. When it becomes constant, overwhelming, or disruptive, it can feel impossible to find peace of mind. If you’re living with anxiety, you’re not alone—and with the right care, relief is possible.</p>			<h3>What Anxiety Feels Like\n</h3>		<p>People experiencing anxiety often describe:</p><ul><li><p>Restlessness or feeling “on edge”</p></li><li><p>Racing thoughts or difficulty controlling worry</p></li><li><p>Physical symptoms like rapid heartbeat, sweating, or stomach upset</p></li><li><p>Difficulty sleeping or relaxing</p></li><li><p>Trouble focusing at work or in daily life</p></li></ul><p><br />Anxiety shows up differently for everyone, but its impact is always real.</p>', 'Anxiety', '', 'inherit', 'closed', 'closed', '', '19-revision-v1', '', '', '2026-02-04 13:43:59', '2026-02-04 13:43:59', '', 19, 'http://localhost/zeliigcaretheme/?p=177', 0, 'revision', '', 0),
